.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt QSTAR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qstar
.Nd standalone QStar build graph evaluator and local executor
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -file Ar qstar.lua
.Op Fl G Ar stella|ninja|auto
.Op Fl B Ar path
.Op Fl -color Ar auto|always|never
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Ar docs
.Op Fl -path | Fl -ai-index | Fl -show Ar wiki-relative.md
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
evaluates QStar authoring files, validates a target graph, renders command
plans, and runs a limited local executor for build, test, install, stage, and
external smoke actions.
The project entrypoint is
.Pa qstar.lua .
Subdirectory fragments use the
.Pa .qst
suffix.
Helper modules use the
.Pa .qsm
suffix and are imported through
.Ic qstar.import_module .
.Pp
QStar is a generic build system.
C, C++, and assembler are supported through language namespaces and explicit
toolsets. Other languages can participate through generated object artifacts.
Generated actions use
.Ic qstar.cli
argv vectors, not shell strings.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--generator"
.It Fl -file Ar qstar.lua
Select the root QStar entrypoint.
.It Fl G Ar stella|ninja|auto
Select the effective generator.
In this release,
.Ar auto
resolves to
.Ar stella .
.Ar stella
runs the local Stella executor.
.Ar ninja
emits and runs a Ninja backend for C/C++/ASM compile, generated actions,
static libraries, executable/test links, run target wrappers, and group phony
targets.
Stage and install copy/manifest work is still performed by QStar, but referenced
target artifacts are built through the effective generator.
.It Fl -generator Ar stella|ninja|auto
Alias for
.Fl G .
.It Fl B Ar path
Override
.Ic qstar.project
build_dir with a package-relative build directory.
.It Fl -color Ar auto|always|never
Control ANSI color for text output.
JSON diagnostics are never colorized.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "list-targets"
.It Ic version
Print the QStar version. The
.Fl -version
form is equivalent.
.It Ic docs
Print local documentation entrypoints, including the wiki and AI index.
Use
.Fl -show
to print a specific wiki document such as
.Pa reference/modules.md .
.It Ic list-targets
List graph targets. Use
.Fl -format Ar json
for the stable machine-readable target listing, including effective generator,
build_dir, generated_dir, compile_commands policy, configs, and installability.
.It Ic query
Print one target, generated action, stage, or config by label.
.It Ic doctor
Inspect toolset resolution, external tools, response file policy, depfile
behavior, and writable build state.
.It Ic check
Evaluate the graph and validate packages, labels, generated outputs, sources,
headers, toolsets, and file inputs without running build actions.
.It Ic lint
Evaluate authoring diagnostics without executing build actions.
.It Ic fmt
Format
.Pa qstar.lua ,
.Pa .qst ,
or
.Pa .qsm
files. Use
.Fl -check
for verification and
.Fl -stdout
to print the formatted text.
.It Ic explain
Print target closure and command-plan information.
.It Ic dry-run
Render action plans without running them.
.It Ic emit-ninja
Emit
.Pa build/qstar/ninja/build.ninja
and the policy-controlled
.Pa compile_commands.json
without running Ninja.
The Ninja backend lowers C/C++/ASM compile actions,
.Ic qstar.configure_file ,
.Ic qstar.custom_target ,
static libraries, shared libraries on macOS and Linux platform contexts,
executable/test links, and
.Ic qstar.run_target
wrappers, plus
.Ic qstar.group
phony targets.
Stage/install copy and manifest actions remain QStar-owned.
Shared library consumers receive build-tree
.Ar @loader_path
or
.Ar $ORIGIN
rpath flags on macOS and Linux.
Windows DLL/import-library/PDB shared library policy is deferred.
.It Ic build
Build using the effective generator.
The
.Ar stella
generator runs the local Stella executor.
The
.Ar ninja
generator emits
.Pa build/qstar/ninja/build.ninja
and invokes
.Xr ninja 1
for the supported MVP graph.
Build accepts
.Fl -jobs Ar N ,
.Fl -schedule-trace ,
.Fl -verbose ,
.Fl -quiet ,
and
.Fl -progress Ar auto|plain|off .
Beta opt-in daemon clients also accept
.Fl -use-daemon Ar auto|never|always
and
.Fl -daemon-socket Ar path .
The daemon path is opt-in and not the default; normal
.Ar stella
build behavior is unchanged.
Default output is compact progress plus the final build summary.
Verbose output adds status lines and
.Li build_action
events, and schedule trace enables deterministic scheduler events.
.Pp
The QStar 0.5 progress contract uses CMake-style action descriptions:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[  8%] Building C object build/qstar/out/__core/obj0.o
[ 75%] Linking CXX executable app
[100%] Built target app
.Ed
.Pp
General output must not expose legacy scheduler stage wording,
.Li Status: compiling ,
.Li schedule_action ,
or
.Li build_action
records.
Those details belong to
.Fl -verbose
or
.Fl -schedule-trace .
Stella observes child stdout/stderr line by line and highlights the
.Li warning:
prefix in orange/yellow. It highlights the
.Li error:
prefix in bold red.
.Fl -color Ar never
and non-TTY output disable ANSI color, and JSON diagnostics remain uncolored.
.It Ic daemon
Run the beta opt-in persistent Stella daemon lifecycle, check a daemon socket,
or query the read-only IDE/AI API.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qstar daemon --socket build/qstar/stella/daemon/qstar-daemon.sock --start
qstar daemon --socket build/qstar/stella/daemon/qstar-daemon.sock --stop
qstar daemon --socket build/qstar/stella/daemon/qstar-daemon.sock --serve
qstar daemon --socket build/qstar/stella/daemon/qstar-daemon.sock --status
qstar daemon --socket build/qstar/stella/daemon/qstar-daemon.sock --query targets.list
.Ed
.Pp
This is not a stable public surface yet. The Q144 MVP keeps Graph IR and the
lowered plan cache result in process memory. Q146 streams daemon build output as
progress, diagnostic, action, summary, and raw output events. The CLI hides
protocol frames and renders the same CMake-style progress and warning/error
color policy as normal Stella builds. If the stream starts and then terminates
before a final status, the client reports daemon stream interruption and does
not silently rerun the build through fallback. Q147 keeps compact dirty-check
and discovered-dependency state in process memory for daemon builds, while
continuing to write
.Pa state/state.db
and
.Pa state/deps.db
as crash-recovery state. Q148 adds macOS
.Li kqueue
and Linux
.Li inotify
file watcher invalidation. When the watcher is active, authoring changes reload
the graph from watcher events instead of first repeating the full authoring
fingerprint scan. If the watcher is unavailable or incomplete, the daemon falls
back to the existing fingerprint scan. Source/header watcher events are traced as
dirty-check invalidation signals; existing Stella dirty-check state still decides
which actions rebuild. Schedule trace output includes
.Li dirty_state_memory
and
.Li deps_memory
hit/miss/writeback lines, plus
.Li daemon_watcher
active/event/unavailable lines.
.Pp
Q150 adds read-only daemon queries for IDE/AI integration:
.Li hello ,
.Li workspace.info ,
.Li targets.list ,
.Li diagnostics.list ,
.Li compile_commands.path ,
and
.Li build.summary .
These queries do not execute build/test/clean actions and return JSON.
Q151 and the 0.6 beta line classify the daemon as a documented beta opt-in
feature. The default
build path remains normal Stella, Windows named pipe support is deferred, and
socket files are local-only and owner-only. Package root or build directory
mismatch is rejected instead of hidden by fallback. Q154 adds background
.Fl -start
and
.Fl -stop
with pid and lock sidecar files, while default-on lifecycle policy remains
deferred.
.Pp
Action descriptions are also preserved in action-log and replay metadata.
.Ic qstar action-log ,
.Ic qstar replay ,
and
.Ic qstar last-failure
print the same
.Li description=
metadata used by progress output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
description='Building C object build/qstar/out/___app/obj0.o'
.Ed
For the Stella executor, successful and cache-hit action
.Pa .log
files are not a public contract. They may be lazily reconstructed from
compact state and the current graph when
.Ic action-log
or
.Ic replay
is requested. Failed actions and the last-failure replay are still written
immediately.
.It Ic test
Build and run QStar test targets.
.It Ic install
Build a target artifact if needed, copy it into a prefix, and write install
manifest state. Use
.Fl -dry-run
to preview the copy plan.
.It Ic stage
Create a copy-only staged package tree.
.It Ic why-rebuild
Explain cache state and why a target would rebuild.
.It Ic clean
Remove the effective build directory, or a single target output with
.Fl -target Ar label .
.It Ic log
Print the latest logical action log paths for a target.
.It Ic last-failure
Print the latest failure replay file and action description metadata.
.It Ic action-log
Print argv/env/input/output log and description metadata for an action id.
.It Ic replay
Print the replay command and description metadata for an action id.
.It Ic lsp
Run the QStar language server with
.Fl -stdio .
.It Ic init
Create a starter project from a generic project shape:
.Ar app ,
.Ar lib ,
.Ar tool ,
.Ar empty ,
or
.Ar workspace .
Use
.Fl -name
to override the project name,
.Fl -use-language
to select the scaffold language, and
.Fl -dry-run
to preview the plan without writing files.
.It Ic --dump-graph
Print the raw Graph IR for debugging and drift tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md"
.It Pa qstar.lua
Project root entrypoint.
.It Pa *.qst
QStar fragment file.
.It Pa *.qsm
QStar helper module file.
.It Pa build/qstar
Default state, log, response file, build artifact, stage, and compile database
directory.
.It Pa generated
Default
.Ic qstar.project
generated_dir for generated action outputs.
.It Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/README.md
Installed QStar wiki entrypoint.
.It Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md
Short documentation map for AI agents and automation.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "QSTAR_DOC_DIR"
.It Ev QSTAR_DOC_DIR
Overrides the documentation directory printed by
.Nm
.Ic docs .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qstar-lua 5 ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/README.md ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/AI_INDEX.md
